# Arik, barkeep of the Blood of the Vine (docs/voice/arik.md)

~ start
Arik: Wine.
-> menu

~ menu
* A cup, then. (1 gp) -> wine
* Who's the man drinking alone by the hearth? -> ismark
* Do you have rooms? -> rooms
* Where does the wine come from? -> source
* Has anyone else come through lately? Travelers? -> travelers
* [Insight DC 12] Study him properly. -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* Goodbye. -> END

~ wine
gold -1
Narrator: The wine is thin, sour and faintly purple, like a bruise you can drink.
interject tag:blunt: Had worse. Not recently.
Arik: Wine.
-> menu

~ ismark
if flag.ismark_met
Arik: Your friend. The Lesser.
else
set ismark_the_lesser_heard
Arik: Ismark. Burgomaster's son. Folk say the Lesser.
endif
-> menu

~ rooms
Arik: Upstairs. Locks work.
interject tag:cheerful: Good locks? I could check them for you. Professionally. For free!
Arik: Locks work.
-> menu

~ source
if flag.wine_shortage_heard
Arik: Still none.
else
set wine_shortage_heard
Arik: Wizard of Wines. No cask in three weeks. Last barrel.
interject class:fighter: A tavern running dry. That's how you know a siege is going badly.
endif
-> menu

~ travelers
if flag.scholar_notes_found
Arik: Scholar. You found the bag.
else
Arik: Scholar. Wrote a lot. Went up the castle road. Left a bag. Back room.
interject name:silvain_aster: Thin, ink to the elbows, never finished a sentence without a footnote? Aurel. It has to be Aurel. Back room, he says. Back room.
endif
-> menu

~ insight_ok
set arik_hollow_noticed
Narrator: You look for whatever looks back out of a man's eyes. There is nothing there. Not cruelty, not grief, not boredom: a clean, empty room with the lamp left on.
-> menu

~ insight_fail
Narrator: A barkeep, polishing a cup. If he has depths, they are very well hidden.
-> menu
